From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:06:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: each page gets a JavaScript heap of its own

The browser window had one JavaScript heap and every page in it a thread
of that heap.  The interface prototypes (Document.prototype, ...) belong
to the heap, so what one page's scripts put on them stayed for the next
page.  On YouTube a search from the home page loaded the results page,
whose Custom Elements polyfill took the last page's replaced
createElement for the native one and recursed until the stack ran out
("stack overflow" thirty times, an unusable page).  Each page now gets
a new heap, freed with its thread.
---
 netsurf/desktop/browser_window.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/netsurf/desktop/browser_window.c b/netsurf/desktop/browser_window.c
index c70db7c..d276128 100644
--- a/netsurf/desktop/browser_window.c
+++ b/netsurf/desktop/browser_window.c
@@ -1602,9 +1602,23 @@ browser_window_callback(hlcache_handle *c, const hlcache_event *event, void *pw)
 			 * window requires a new javascript thread object
 			 */
 			jsthread *thread;
+			jsheap *heap = NULL;
 			assert(bw->loading_content == c);
 
-			if (js_newthread(bw->jsheap,
+			/* each page gets a heap of its own: the interface
+			 * prototypes (Document.prototype, ...) belong to the
+			 * heap, and with one heap per window what a page's
+			 * scripts put on them stayed for the next page (a
+			 * Custom Elements polyfill took the last page's
+			 * createElement for the native one and recursed until
+			 * the stack ran out).  The heap goes with the thread:
+			 * one marked for destruction goes when its last thread
+			 * does. */
+			if (js_newheap(nsoption_int(script_timeout),
+					&heap) != NSERROR_OK)
+				heap = NULL;
+
+			if (js_newthread(heap != NULL ? heap : bw->jsheap,
 					 bw,
 					 hlcache_handle_get_content(c),
 					 &thread) == NSERROR_OK) {
@@ -1614,6 +1628,8 @@ browser_window_callback(hlcache_handle *c, const hlcache_event *event, void *pw)
 				 */
 				*(event->data.jsthread) = thread;
 			}
+			if (heap != NULL)
+				js_destroyheap(heap);
 		}
 		break;
 
